.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "fuzzygene_export_trace" "fuzzygene_export_trace"
.SH NAME
fuzzygene_export_trace \- Export the two trajectory matrices of one virtual perturbation to a folder.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIfuzzygene_export_trace(\fBfuzzygene\fR as <generic> FuzzyGeneModel, 
\fBgene\fR as string, 
\fBdir\fR as string, 
\fBmode\fR as string = "knockout", 
\fBsteps\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBdt\fR as double = 1, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Export the two trajectory matrices of one virtual perturbation to a folder.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfuzzygene\fB \fR\- a trained (or restored) model. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgene\fB \fR\- the target gene of the virtual perturbation. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdir\fB \fR\- the output folder (created when missing). 
.PP
.PP
\fBmode\fB \fR\- \fBknockout\fR (default), \fBknockdown\fR or \fBoverexpression\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsteps\fB \fR\- maximum iteration steps; 0 uses the model configuration. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdt\fB \fR\- time unit of one iteration frame, used by the sidecar only. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment used to report errors. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a character vector of the written file paths
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
Writes, into **dir**:
 


 
- \fBtrace.mutant.csv\fR / \fBtrace.wildtype.csv\fR: gene x iteration matrices;
- \fB*.sampleinfo.json\fR: one `SampleInfo` row per column (\fBtime\fR / \fBiteration\fR
 / \fBomega\fR / \fBconverged\fR / \fBperturbed_genes\fR ...), ready for the ExperimentDesigner
 pipeline;
- \fBtrace.perturbation.json\fR: the run summary plus the whole \fBmax_delta\fR sequence.


 


 \fBdt\fR only affects \fBmetadata$time\fR of the sidecar (`time = iteration * dt`); it does
 not change the matrix. Leave it at 1 unless the model is a lagged (time series) model and
 the sampling interval is known.
 


 
\fB
 let files = FuzzyGene::fuzzygene_export_trace(model, "TPPP3", "/path/trace", mode = "knockout");
 print(files);
 
\fR`
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
FuzzyGene
